WEBVTT

1
00:00:02.700 --> 00:00:05.182
A stream job counts payments per card.

2
00:00:05.182 --> 00:00:11.844
Two sources read payment events from Kafka, a counter adds them up, and a sink writes the results out.

3
00:00:12.000 --> 00:00:16.155
Each source keeps an offset: how far it has read into its log.

4
00:00:16.155 --> 00:00:19.640
Both are at 7, and the counter has counted 9 so far.

5
00:00:19.640 --> 00:00:21.449
Five more are on their way.

6
00:00:21.633 --> 00:00:24.784
If the machine dies, the count in memory is gone.

7
00:00:24.784 --> 00:00:29.092
Recovery needs a saved count, and the offsets from the same moment.

8
00:00:29.300 --> 00:00:31.655
Stopping the job to save would stall it.

9
00:00:31.655 --> 00:00:34.775
So the snapshot is taken while payments keep flowing.

10
00:00:34.967 --> 00:00:36.291
Checkpoint 1 starts.

11
00:00:36.291 --> 00:00:45.497
Each source writes down its offset, 7 and 7, and sends a marker called a barrier down its channel, behind the payments it has already sent.

12
00:00:45.667 --> 00:00:52.073
A barrier never overtakes a payment, so it splits each channel in two: before the checkpoint, and after.

13
00:00:52.267 --> 00:00:55.039
Source 0's barrier reaches the counter first.

14
00:00:55.039 --> 00:01:01.261
The counter stops reading that input, because payments 7 and 8 behind it belong after the checkpoint.

15
00:01:01.433 --> 00:01:05.350
It keeps reading the other input until that barrier arrives too.

16
00:01:05.350 --> 00:01:07.185
This wait is called alignment.

17
00:01:07.400 --> 00:01:13.638
Now the counter has counted 14, seven from each source, the same as the saved offsets.

18
00:01:13.638 --> 00:01:16.395
It saves 14 and passes the barrier on.

19
00:01:16.567 --> 00:01:19.273
The sink holds its writes in a transaction.

20
00:01:19.273 --> 00:01:24.687
When the barrier reaches it, checkpoint 1 is complete and the sink commits 14 updates.

21
00:01:24.833 --> 00:01:28.076
The counter reaches 17, and then the machine dies.

22
00:01:28.076 --> 00:01:32.292
The count, the channels and the sink's open transaction are lost.

23
00:01:32.533 --> 00:01:36.365
Kafka still has the input, and storage has checkpoint 1.

24
00:01:36.365 --> 00:01:40.333
The counter loads 14, and each source rewinds to offset 7.

25
00:01:40.500 --> 00:01:45.542
Payments 7 and up go through a second time, but none of them were in the 14.

26
00:01:45.542 --> 00:01:48.727
Each one counts once, and the count is 17 again.

27
00:01:48.900 --> 00:01:51.171
Some payments were processed twice.

28
00:01:51.171 --> 00:01:52.988
Each one still counted once.
